traffic-count (2.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Sample the BPF counters every live_interval (new config key, default
    1 s) for /api/v1/live; the database is still written every
    flush_interval (10 s), so there are no extra writes.
  * /api/v1/live reports the live interval instead of the last flush time.

 -- KexiChan Project <kexi@example.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

traffic-count (2.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Count per device from the LAN device's point of view: upload is keyed on
    the Ethernet source of ingress frames, download on the destination of
    egress frames. Previously the router's own MAC absorbed most traffic.
  * Per-CPU LRU counters with a zeroed key; no lost updates, no padding junk.
  * In-memory baseline instead of SQLite checkpoints: no double counting after
    midnight or restarts, no uint64 wrap-around.
  * Days follow the configured time zone; interface names are recorded.
  * Re-attach automatically when an interface is re-created; fall back to
    clsact/cls_bpf on kernels without TCX; never short-circuit other tc users.
  * BPF object embedded in the binary; no clang/libbpf needed on the target.
  * Config keys are snake_case as documented (they were silently ignored).
  * New API: sorted /api/v1/traffic, /api/v1/summary, /api/v1/series,
    /api/v1/live. New SQLite tables; v1 tables are left untouched.

 -- KexiChan Project <kexi@example.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

